      "reading": "The PTS-only timestamp carries another prefix",
      "clause": "H.222.0 \u00a7\u00a72.4.3.6\u20132.4.3.7 Table 2-21 requires prefix 0010 for PTS without DTS.",
      "candidate": "Refuses the timestamp header when the prefix does not match its flags.",
      "reference": "Delivers 17 payload bytes at 180000 ticks.",
      "compat": "compat::pes::IgnoreTimestampPrefix",
      "cases": [
        "wrong-time-prefix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "TEI and an incomplete finite PES",
      "clause": "H.222.0 \u00a7\u00a72.4.3.3 and 2.4.3.7 define TEI and the exact finite PES packet length. The fault recovery policy requires the entire PES.",
      "candidate": "Refuses without a complete finite PES.",
      "reference": "Delivers the available 17 bytes with a corrupt flag.",
      "compat": "compat::pes::DeliverCorruptPrefix",
      "cases": [
        "tei-incomplete-finite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "A zero-length PES belongs to a selected audio PID",
      "clause": "H.222.0 \u00a72.4.3.7 allows PES_packet_length zero only for video elementary payload in TS, and the fault adapter is scoped to AVC.",
      "candidate": "Refuses the AAC route for this recovery profile.",
      "reference": "Returns the nonconforming 27-byte audio payload.",
      "compat": "compat::pes::AllowUnboundedAudio",
      "cases": [
        "pes-audio-zero-length-invalid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "A terminal transport error has carriers after it",
      "clause": "H.222.0 \u00a7\u00a72.4.3.2\u20132.4.3.3 define fixed transport packet geometry. The terminal fault policy requires the damaged carrier to reach the physical end.",
      "candidate": "Publishes the initial intact packet and refuses confirmation of terminal transport loss while more physical input follows.",
      "reference": "Publishes the same packet and ends cleanly.",
      "compat": "compat::input::ResyncTransport",
      "cases": [
        "valid-transport-sync-loss-then-valid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "No applicable PAT routes the following PES",
